Marsi ac Peligni simul convenientes, positis insidiis
in <NOTE N="1636" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0563" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0563"></COL> in l. a  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  1 <SUP>b</SUP> . 2.</NOTE>  locis artissimis, irruerunt viriliter <NOTE N="1637" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0563" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0563"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0564B"></COL> super eos, et universos fere interficientes, ingentem
nimis praedam in auro et argento ac <NOTE N="1638" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0563" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0563"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . Reliqua post</HI>  palliis  <HI REND="ITALIC">abscisa sunt</HI>  1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  palliis <NOTE N="1639" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0563" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0563"></COL> p. ac tapetis
